      "content": "Retributive justice is a moral framework that relies on the idea of \"just deserts,\" but it is fundamentally flawed because it assumes suffering is the only valid form of justice, which is a cruel and outdated view. True justice should focus on healing and restoring relationships, not inflicting pain, because a system built on vengeance perpetuates cycles of violence rather than solving the root causes of crime. Prioritizing rehabilitation and victim empowerment over retribution is the only way to build a society that values human dignity and long-term safety over short-term satisfaction.",
      "source": "target",
